<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick II of Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1534–1588</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from 1559. In his first year he bought the bishoprics of Ösel-Wiek and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a> for his younger brother Magnus of Holstein, drawing Denmark into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>. He fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-seven-years-war">Northern Seven Years' War</a> of 1563–1570, rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kronborg">Kronborg</a> castle at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helsingor">Helsingør</a>, and gave the astronomer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tycho-brahe">Tycho Brahe</a> the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ven-island">Hven</a> for his observatory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="Frederick II of Denmark" width="320" height="638" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Knieper · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1581_Frederik_2..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
